⚽
"Letter Pile"/en
=== start
¶Five big letters tumble into a pile, then hearts and soccer balls rain down
and settle into their bowls and hooks. The letters and hearts collide by the
shape of their outlines rather than by the rectangles around them, which is
what lets a ball come to rest inside the bowl of a letter instead of floating
above it, and a heart wedge its point between two letters.¶

¶A heavy display face, because a fat letter has a bowl wide enough to catch a
ball. The letters are chosen for their hooks and bowls.¶
face: "Titan One"
letters: ['a' 'b' 'c' 'd' 'e']

¶The letters drop first, from the same place but staggered heights, so each one
lands on the last and the pile builds upward.

A letter is solid only because its place is a Motion and it has Matter — output
that a program places is a ghost that everything passes through. Their mass is
what keeps the balls from shoving the pile apart, and asking Matter for an
outline is what makes them collide by their letterforms.¶
pile: letters.translate(
	ƒ(letter•'' index•#)
		Phrase(
			letter
			4m
			face
			name: "letter\index\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(((index × 0.6m) - 1.5m) ((index × 6m) + 1m))
			)
			color: Color(75% 80 (index × 62°))
			matter: Matter(mass: 60kg friction: 0.9 outline: ⊤)
		)
)

¶The hearts fall next. An emoji can ask for its outline too, so each heart
collides by its shape: its point slips into the gaps a box would sit on top of.¶
hearts: ['🧡' '💛' '💚' '💙' '💜' '🩷'].translate(
	ƒ(heart•'' index•#)
		Phrase(
			heart
			2m
			name: "heart\index\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(((index × 0.9m) - 2.5m) ((index × 1.5m) + 27m))
			)
			matter: Matter(mass: 20kg friction: 0.8 outline: ⊤)
		)
)

¶The balls start above everything, so they arrive after the pile has settled.
They don't ask for an outline: their rectangle, rounded all the way, is what
makes them roll.¶
balls: 18 → [].translate(
	ƒ(number)
		Phrase(
			"⚽"
			1.1m
			name: "ball\number\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(Random(-3m 3m) ((number × 1.8m) + 34m))
				Velocity(Random(-1m/s 1m/s) 0m/s)
			)
			matter: Matter(bounciness: 0.3 friction: 0.4 roundedness: 0.5)
		)
)

Stage(
	[
		¶A shallow valley to settle in, and two walls. The floor is a Path
		rather than a Rectangle because a barrier is always slippery — it keeps
		the friction Matter.js gave it — so a flat one would let the pile slide
		into a corner instead of gathering under the falling balls.¶
		Shape(Path([Place(-6m -2.5m) Place(0m -5.5m) Place(6m -2.5m)]))
		Shape(Rectangle(-7m 10m -6m -6m))
		Shape(Rectangle(6m 10m 7m -6m))
		:pile
		:hearts
		:balls
	]
	gravity: 9.8m/s^2
	place: Place(0m 1m -10m)
	background: Color(25% 20 250°)
)
